% SCHERZO, reprise of the first part, bars 105-140.
% c022: 111 viola B+A, Hn 1 B, Hn 2 F sharp (no augmented 2nd C-D sharp); 125-126 bass C-B, Bsn 1 E-D sharp: iv6-V (Phrygian) instead of the augmented 2nd C-D sharp in the bass (A-S PDF 168-169, 171 Ex. 11-14).
% 105-120: theme A ff, tutti: Vln I with Fl 1-2 and Ob 1 at pitch, Cl 1 and Vln II an octave lower; horns on beats 1 and 3,
%   trumpets in motive x (a fanfare figure only: the trumpets have no melody in the scherzo; cyclic-notes), timpani with the bass.
% 121-132: the second idea in E minor (it was in G major at 45), hemiola.
% c063: 121 sub. p after the ff tutti, strings first (Fl 1 and Ob 1 rest 121-124 and enter 125), crescendo 125-128 to f at the hemiola cadence 129:
%   the restatement takes a new colour and level instead of a fourth loud arrival in a row (Adler II PDF 257-258 dialogue; 190 forte subito piano; 267 the
%   orchestra reduced when the solo line enters after the tutti; 288 the doubling changed in the second phrase). The 16-bar ff block 105-120 now gives way.
% 133-140: close: motive x in the cellos, dying away to E minor pp.
% c023: timpani E pp at 139 with the basses' E (was 138, under the cellos' V F sharp-D sharp-B).

% c036: 109-112 and 117-120 Fl 1 an octave above Fl 2, as at 309-312 and 317-320 in the reprise: two flutes in unison on E5/B4 add little in a ff tutti
% (Adler PDF 174, 185: 'sweet and with little carrying power'; the register from E6 is 'clear and brilliant'); 108 beat 3 rest for the leap, as at 308
% c052: 105 Fl 1 G5 on beat 1 (was E5 with the theme): the soprano seventh A5 of the V7 at 104 resolves by step in its own register; Vln I leaps to the theme's E5
%   (A-S PDF 406-407 sec. 9, Ex. 24-11: a transferred resolution needs the tone of resolution in the same register).
